      "content": "I hear you—thirty years of work erased isn't a phase, it's a verdict. But \"fundamentally destroyed\" is a story you're telling yourself, not a fact. The blueprint you can't find isn't gone; it's buried under the rubble of your own grief. You don't have to rebuild the same thing—you get to build something that fits the person you are now, not the one you were. And that starts with one small, ugly, unglamorous step, not a grand vision.",
